after another huge brawl and face-off  the ending of kobrakai season 5 leaves  the future of john crease's karate dojo  in enormous doubt and perhaps signals  the imminent end of the series itself  yupikai movie lovers i'm jan and in this  video i'm explaining how cobra kai's  fifth season could be setting up a big  twist in season six plus i'll be  revealing the little details and easter  eggs you might have missed in the season  5 finale spoilers ahead of course so  take care  season 5 ends with a smashing showdown  as daniel triumphs over silver crane  kicking him through a giant glass cobra  as silver students line up to quit and  throw off their kobrakai shirts in  disgust after the revelation their  sensei bribed the referee at the all  valley tournaments in season four it  appears that kobrakai's days may truly  be numbered interestingly daniel defeats  the sneaky sensei by employing against  him the quicksilver rules that silva  taught him in karate kid 3. this is  exactly what chosen recommended to  daniel in the very first episode to  catch serpent you must think like  serpent we will use his style against  him daniel's victory here shows he's  been willing to embrace other karate  styles in addition to those he learned  from mr miyagi something he admitted to  johnny at the end of season 4 when he  saw his own daughter using some of eagle  fang's moves at the tournament but i see  some of what you teach can be good  sometimes this continues the overarching  cobra kai series theme of former foes  reconciling and then making something  new by blending their contrasting  attitudes and styles of karate together  we've combined our different styles to  train our students into the best  fighters i've ever seen by the way  notice that the way daniel lands his  final blow on silva by crane kicking him  into the glass cobra on the wall behind  him is a callback to when silva fell  into a pane of glass during the fight  with mr miyagi in the karate kid 3 as  well as to daniel's winning kick to take  out the young cobra kai star johnny in  the original movie but let's not forget  the crucial part the miyagido students  also played in taking down silva after  uncovering the incriminating footage of  tory's talk with her sensei they  remembered chosen's training and advice  to work together as a team against the  onslaught of cobra kai he said that the  snakes will take us down one by one but  what if we weren't a bunch of once the  only way we win is if we work together  similar to how together they surrounded  the basket of eggs to protect it against  chosen they formed a barrier around  anthony and the tablet which was  uploading the incriminating clip of  silva so by the end of season 5 with the  exception of crease more on him shortly  the biggest cobra kaya miyagido  rivalries appear to have been resolved  for both the og karate kid characters  and the new generation miguel and robbie  are now friends sam and tori are  reconciled and fought together against  sensei kim with devon also abandoning  cobra kai to join them oh i will be a  champion but i'll get there my way not  yours meanwhile kenny's beef with robbie  seems to have been put aside and even  stingray redeems himself when he comes  to rescue daniel what are you doing it's  pitch blackout stingray see better in  the dark but with silver hauled off by  the police what's left now for the  series and the kobrakai legacy he  repeatedly spoke about in season five i  never had any children my only legacy is  cobra guy well conveniently in season  five we're introduced to the  granddaughter of master kim who silva  invited over from korea to join him at  cobra kai i did not get on the plane for  manu what i'm offering you is legacy  your grandfather didn't teach american  soldiers the way of the fist just to use  on the battlefield we have to share his  style with the world as a child she  avidly watched the young crease and  silver train with her grandfather and  she's clearly motivated to make her own  mark in the martial arts world now silva  may be arrested but kobrakai as a dojo  was already accepted to compete at the  sekai taikai international tournament  and if she wanted she could recruit her  own students perhaps from korea and  enter the competition under the kobrakai  name thus continuing the legacy of  kobrakai fulfilling what silva predicted  cobra kai will go on forever though of  course it's also possible that she'd  want to distance herself from the bad  publicity surrounding silver and his  dojo the sekai tai kai tournament will  undoubtedly be the focus of season six  and it seems more than likely that  sensei kim will be competing there in  some form or another bringing her  grandfather's way of the fist style of  fighting to the competition and setting  up a clash with the karate styles  championed by daniel and johnny at  miyagidou and eagle fang chosen also  revealed that his uncle sato the  secondary villain from karate kid 2 had  major beef with master kim and i expect  a lot of that history will be revealed  in season six setting up a collision  between chosen and sensei kim my uncle  sato did not speak much of kim sung yang  but i know he had much anger towards him  chosen also revealed that master kim's  teachings are behind a lot of cobra  kai's brutal philosophy kim sung young  styro is based on deception no honor no  mercy of course john crease the og big  bad of the original karate kid film  we'll be back to mix things up in season  six after faking his own death yet again  the finale began with crease pretending  he was done with everything after being  tricked by his former star student  johnny an arch enemy daniel and telling  tory to look after herself from now on  and forget about him and his opening  words in the final episode this is it  end of the line a recall back to what  dany's mum said to her teen son when  they first arrived in la the event that  kicked off the whole karate kid and  kobrakai saga this is it this is the end  of the line that's a clever little  signal that although crease claims he's  giving up this moment is really just the  beginning of a new chapter in his life  just like it was for daniel all those  years ago now that an unrepentant crease  has broken out of prison it'll be  interesting to see how he reacts to  silva's arrest and discovering that the  students from his beloved dojo have  abandoned it the threat that johnny made  to wipe out kris's legacy appears to  have come true you want to know why i'm  in this fight so i can erase everything  you did every mark you left every memory  of you i expect kris might well team up  with sensei kim when he discovers she's  been at cobra kai remember from the  flashback that they both seemed to get  along with each other when they were  younger and this will be kris's  opportunity to re-establish the legacy  of kobrakai which of course came from  kim's grandfather on top of that going  up against daniel and johnny at the  international tournament will be a  chance for him to get revenge on them  for the trick they pulled on him in  prison i think kris will also be looking  to get his own personal payback on silva  for framing him for beating up stingray  first of all i'm not entirely convinced  silva will be going to jail he's got  plenty of money to pay the best lawyers  around and they could probably convince  the jury that stingray's new testimony  is unreliable given he already lied  about kris plus the video evidence of  silver beating up stingray has already  been deleted if silva does go free then  crease will likely want his own revenge  there is an endgame kick silver is going  down only he doesn't know it yet now  season six hasn't been confirmed by  netflix yet but apparently some scenes  have already been filmed however my  feeling is that it could well be the  final season of the series many major  character arcs have already been wrapped  up in season five and it's hard to see  how exactly the series could carry on  and top the stakes of the biggest karate  tournament in the world it also makes me  wonder whether there could be a big  surprise twist for the final season and  i think there's a clue in the season 5  moment when daniel and johnny were  accepted in the tournament and were  asked for the name of their dojo we just  need your dojo's name we are miyagido  and we are eagle fang well  which is it now wild and out there  theory time folks but what if johnny and  daniel decide they want to finally  rehabilitate the cobra kind name by  taking on the mantle themselves so that  miyagido and eagle fang combine to  become the new cobra kai or miyagi kobra  fang it was johnny after all who  resurrected cobra kai and it would be an  intriguing turn of events for the og  karate kid to rehabilitate the dojo of  his former nemesis he did already of  course train at silva's kobrakai in the  third movie and used some of those  techniques this season to defeat silva  the biggest problem with this idea is  that it may be hard for daniel to  justify it as fitting in with and  honoring mr miyagi's legacy of course  the whole name thing may just be a bit  of fun and a mess moment alluding to how  fans have referred to daniel and  johnny's team up in earlier seasons as  miyagi fang something also acknowledged  by stingray when he gets ambushed biaggy  things overall i feel that season 6  might be the best way to end the  kobrakai series on a relatively high  note rather than dragging things out for  many more seasons so what do you think  did you enjoy season 5 and do you think  the series is ready to wrap things up  for good in season six you can tap here  for more kobrakai videos with easter  eggs and details you missed and if you  liked this video do leave a thumbs up i  really appreciate it thanks for enjoying  cobra kai with me and hope you have a  marvellous movie loving week yippie kai  movie lovers
 

